  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 4.2. Strengthened capacity of enterprises to adopt new business models, technology and techniques to enhance productivity and sustainability</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through a partnership between the State Employment Service (SES), the Ministry of Education, and education and training institutions and providers, a new on-line platform provides young women and men with access to entrepreneurship training. With the contribution of the Government of the Czech Republic, the Government of Denmark, and own resources (RBTC), the ILO has supported the expansion of opportunities for young women and men to access entrepreneurship training. Parallel to the efforts to institutionalise Start and Improve Your Business (SIYB) across public and private organizations, the ILO has facilitated the adaptation of the ILO&#x2019;s &#x2018;Biz Up&#x2019; training to the Ukrainian context. Through a partnership with the ILO&#x2019;s International Training Centre (ITC), an on-line training platform was set up to support access by young women and men to this training in spite of the prevailing epidemiological circumstances. Training of trainers (ToT) activities took place both through webinars and in person (with around 40 participants from the Ministry of Education, State employment service, business trainers and NGOs). 

Over 100 women benefitted from SIYB trainings under the joint programme with UNDP. Overall, over 1,300 beneficiaries in Ukraine were trained on SIYB (of which 65 per cent were women) thanks to the ILO&#x2019;s technical assistance and the pooling of funds from multiple sources.</narrative>
   </description>
